WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:06.753
Five years ago,

00:00:06.753 --> 00:00:08.672
I was on this stage

00:00:08.713 --> 00:00:12.592
to talk about the relationships
between humans and machines.

00:00:13.552 --> 00:00:18.223
Today, I'm here to talk only
about the relationships between humans.

00:00:19.266 --> 00:00:21.142
I regularly say

00:00:21.184 --> 00:00:24.563
in my lectures on artificial intelligence

00:00:24.604 --> 00:00:28.108
that humans will always have
a monopoly on evil.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.735
It's not a threat,

00:00:30.777 --> 00:00:34.155
just a reminder that people choose.

00:00:34.197 --> 00:00:35.949
We are not algorithms.

00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:42.122
We are not bound by code
or commandments or laws or treaties.

00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:43.290
We have them.

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:45.625
But we choose.

00:00:46.626 --> 00:00:51.214
So let us talk now
about the choices we make.

00:00:51.256 --> 00:00:54.509
About things in black and white.

00:00:55.802 --> 00:00:58.221
About Russia's war on Ukraine.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.515
And about good and evil.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:08.023
My life experience prepared me
to identify evil at an early age.

00:01:08.648 --> 00:01:11.651
Not my life as the chess player.

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:15.322
Not even as the youngest
world champion in history.

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:16.531
No.

00:01:16.531 --> 00:01:20.619
My relevant experience
is where I was born and raised,

00:01:21.453 --> 00:01:27.250
in what Ronald Reagan
accurately called the “evil empire,”

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.585
the USSR.

00:01:29.794 --> 00:01:36.551
As a young star in the chess-crazed
Soviet Union in the ’70s and ’80s,

00:01:36.551 --> 00:01:39.554
I had many privileges
my compatriots did not.

00:01:40.013 --> 00:01:43.850
I could travel to the West
outside of the Iron Curtain,

00:01:43.892 --> 00:01:48.188
where it was obvious to me very quickly

00:01:48.188 --> 00:01:51.358
that they were the free world
and we were not,

00:01:51.399 --> 00:01:54.235
despite what communist propaganda told us.

00:01:56.321 --> 00:02:01.868
I eventually got into trouble
for sharing these views.

00:02:01.910 --> 00:02:05.955
What late American civil rights hero
and Congressman John Lewis

00:02:05.955 --> 00:02:08.291
would have called “good trouble.”

00:02:09.876 --> 00:02:12.879
My criticism of the Soviet system

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:16.299
and my praise for America was bad enough.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:21.763
But it was even worse
because where it was published.

00:02:21.763 --> 00:02:23.556
[“Playboy” Interview: Garry Kasparov]

00:02:23.556 --> 00:02:25.100
(Laughter)

00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:30.855
My comments were almost
as [much of] a scandal

00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:36.653
as Soviet movie star Natalya Negoda’s
nude photos in “Playboy” in the same year.

00:02:38.196 --> 00:02:42.409
I felt I had to speak out

00:02:42.409 --> 00:02:46.329
to use my fame to push
the envelope of free speech

00:02:46.329 --> 00:02:48.998
in Gorbachev's collapsing empire.

00:02:49.457 --> 00:02:53.211
The next year, in October 1990,

00:02:53.253 --> 00:02:57.006
in my world championship match
against Anatoly Karpov in New York City,

00:02:57.048 --> 00:03:00.135
I refused to play
under Soviet hammer and sickle

00:03:00.176 --> 00:03:02.887
and demanded to play under Russian flag.

00:03:05.306 --> 00:03:08.435
The USSR staggered on for another year

00:03:08.476 --> 00:03:13.356
until it disintegrated
on Christmas Day, 1991.

00:03:14.899 --> 00:03:18.278
Oh, what a great moment
in world history.

00:03:19.195 --> 00:03:20.530
How we celebrated,

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:23.658
the evil empire had fallen,
the future looked bright.

00:03:24.492 --> 00:03:30.081
And yet, eight years later,
on December 31, 1999,

00:03:30.123 --> 00:03:36.588
a former lieutenant colonel of the KGB
became the president of Russia.

00:03:36.629 --> 00:03:38.631
His name was Vladimir Putin.

00:03:39.883 --> 00:03:41.301
How this happened

00:03:41.342 --> 00:03:43.428
is a long, painful story.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.808
And in fact, I wrote a book about it
in 2015 called "Winter is Coming."

00:03:50.518 --> 00:03:52.645
Not an original title, I have to admit.

00:03:52.979 --> 00:03:54.481
(Laughter)

00:03:54.522 --> 00:03:59.819
But I'm a fan of "Game of Thrones."

00:03:59.861 --> 00:04:01.571
(Laughter)

00:04:01.613 --> 00:04:06.201
And also I felt it was appropriate
because it was a warning.

00:04:06.785 --> 00:04:08.870
The subtitle was more important:

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.457
"Why Vladimir Putin and the Enemies
of the Free World Must Be Stopped."

00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:15.877
The publisher, by the way, didn't like it.

00:04:15.877 --> 00:04:17.629
"Enemies."

00:04:18.421 --> 00:04:19.589
It's too harsh.

00:04:19.631 --> 00:04:20.965
Sounded like Cold War.

00:04:20.965 --> 00:04:22.133
"Absolutely," I said.

00:04:22.175 --> 00:04:24.552
"Cold War because winter is coming."

00:04:24.594 --> 00:04:25.762
(Laughter)

00:04:26.471 --> 00:04:30.058
Well, here we are, seven years later.

00:04:30.099 --> 00:04:31.851
And if I wrote a sequel,

00:04:31.851 --> 00:04:34.521
it would be called “Winter Is Here.”

00:04:35.688 --> 00:04:40.151
And the subtitle would be
"I Bleeping Told You So."

00:04:40.193 --> 00:04:42.195
(Laughter)

00:04:43.655 --> 00:04:47.283
Actually, my first article of warning

00:04:47.325 --> 00:04:49.327
was published in
“The Wall Street Journal”

00:04:49.369 --> 00:04:51.538
on January 4, 2001.

00:04:53.331 --> 00:04:56.292
I saw evil because I heard evil.

00:04:56.584 --> 00:04:58.711
Putin was telling us what he was.

00:04:58.711 --> 00:05:01.381
All we had to do was listen.

00:05:02.298 --> 00:05:07.971
When Putin said that there was
no such thing as a former KGB agent,

00:05:07.971 --> 00:05:13.184
I knew Russia's fragile
democracy was in danger.

00:05:13.184 --> 00:05:16.729
When Putin said that the collapse
of the Soviet Union

00:05:16.729 --> 00:05:19.691
was the greatest geopolitical
catastrophe of the 20th century,

00:05:19.691 --> 00:05:24.237
I knew Russia’s newly independent
neighbors were at risk.

00:05:25.446 --> 00:05:30.410
And when Putin talked at the Munich
Security Conference in 2007

00:05:30.451 --> 00:05:34.163
about a return to spheres of influence,

00:05:34.205 --> 00:05:37.000
I knew he was ready to launch his plan.

00:05:39.752 --> 00:05:44.173
It was the language from
the Molotov-Ribbentrop Pact, 1939.

00:05:44.215 --> 00:05:48.011
The language Hitler and Stalin
used to divide Europe.

00:05:48.761 --> 00:05:51.639
And a year later, in 2008,

00:05:51.681 --> 00:05:53.600
Putin invaded the Republic of Georgia.

00:05:53.641 --> 00:05:55.643
2014, Ukraine.

00:05:57.395 --> 00:05:59.355
It's a paradox, isn't it?

00:05:59.355 --> 00:06:03.735
Dictators lie about everything
they have done,

00:06:03.776 --> 00:06:07.071
but often they tell us
exactly what they're going to do.

00:06:07.947 --> 00:06:09.449
Just listen.

00:06:10.992 --> 00:06:16.205
Anyone who is surprised
at Putin's war crimes in Ukraine

00:06:16.247 --> 00:06:20.793
must not be aware about his long record,

00:06:20.835 --> 00:06:26.215
beginning with the Second Chechen War
in Grozny more than two decades ago.

00:06:26.257 --> 00:06:30.219
Vladimir Putin has been
a war criminal from the start.

00:06:33.348 --> 00:06:37.101
So in 2005, still being ranked number one,

00:06:37.101 --> 00:06:40.438
I retired from professional chess

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:44.734
to form a pro-democracy,
anti-Putin movement in Russia.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:48.988
As you could see, it didn't go so well.

00:06:50.865 --> 00:06:53.242
But it was not about winning or losing.

00:06:54.911 --> 00:06:57.080
I knew it was my moral duty

00:06:57.121 --> 00:07:00.208
in keeping with the slogan
of Soviet dissidents:

00:07:00.249 --> 00:07:02.502
"Do what you must and so be it."

00:07:03.169 --> 00:07:06.547
Ah, my friends and critics
both kept telling me,

00:07:06.547 --> 00:07:10.093
"Gary, you are a chess player,
you're not a politician.

00:07:10.718 --> 00:07:12.512
This is not chess.

00:07:12.512 --> 00:07:14.764
You see everything in black and white.

00:07:14.764 --> 00:07:16.599
Politics are gray.

00:07:16.599 --> 00:07:18.893
You have to compromise."

00:07:19.769 --> 00:07:20.895
Really?

00:07:21.938 --> 00:07:25.817
Those who peacefully marched
with me for free Russia

00:07:25.858 --> 00:07:28.820
are either in exile, like me.

00:07:28.820 --> 00:07:31.489
Or in jail, like Alexei Navalny.

00:07:31.531 --> 00:07:35.284
Or even murdered like Boris Nemtsov.

00:07:36.202 --> 00:07:37.370
Compromise?

00:07:44.377 --> 00:07:45.586
Not black and white?

00:07:47.463 --> 00:07:48.965
Are you sure?

00:07:48.965 --> 00:07:50.675
Compromise with this?

00:07:51.759 --> 00:07:56.389
You cannot look at the images
from Ukraine in recent weeks

00:07:56.431 --> 00:07:58.516
and say there is no pure evil.

00:08:01.144 --> 00:08:03.271
Mariupol destroyed, Bucha slaughtered,

00:08:03.312 --> 00:08:06.399
Kramatorsk train station massacred.

00:08:07.775 --> 00:08:10.236
And worse is yet to come.

00:08:11.112 --> 00:08:15.408
And these horrors
are not from Poland in 1945.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.203
Not from Rwanda in 1994.

00:08:19.829 --> 00:08:22.582
Not Aleppo 2016.

00:08:22.582 --> 00:08:25.626
This is Europe this week.

00:08:27.837 --> 00:08:29.839
How could this happen?

00:08:30.673 --> 00:08:34.218
How did we forget what evil can do?

00:08:35.219 --> 00:08:40.391
We have lost the generation
that saw World War II firsthand.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:46.022
Otherwise we reserve
absolute evil for fiction.

00:08:53.321 --> 00:08:56.407
In fables, they believe in true evil.

00:08:57.075 --> 00:08:59.202
Good is harder to define.

00:08:59.202 --> 00:09:00.703
There is no pure good.

00:09:01.079 --> 00:09:05.500
If anyone says
they know what pure good is,

00:09:05.541 --> 00:09:06.793
it's probably evil.

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.338
(Laughter)

00:09:13.966 --> 00:09:20.098
In fantasy tales of hobbits
and elves and dwarves,

00:09:20.098 --> 00:09:25.144
there was an idea that good comes
in different forms and shapes,

00:09:25.186 --> 00:09:26.479
often in conflict.

00:09:26.521 --> 00:09:29.774
But they had to be united
when facing absolute evil.

00:09:30.274 --> 00:09:31.901
Good will disagree.

00:09:31.943 --> 00:09:35.238
Evil says, "No more disagreements ever."

00:09:35.863 --> 00:09:39.575
That was life in real Mordor,
the Soviet Union.

00:09:39.617 --> 00:09:43.329
That's what Putin wants
for Russia and the world.

00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:51.212
We celebrated the end of the Cold War,
but for too long,

00:09:51.212 --> 00:09:54.799
we forgot that evil doesn’t die.

00:09:55.925 --> 00:09:59.971
It can be buried for a while
under the rubble of the Berlin Wall,

00:10:00.012 --> 00:10:04.225
but it grows back
through the cracks of our apathy.

00:10:07.019 --> 00:10:10.481
We called it diplomacy

00:10:10.481 --> 00:10:14.735
when Putin was embraced
by the leaders of the free world

00:10:14.777 --> 00:10:17.029
as equal despite his crimes.

00:10:18.531 --> 00:10:21.117
We called it engagement

00:10:21.117 --> 00:10:25.121
when we bought trillions of dollars
in Russian oil and gas,

00:10:25.121 --> 00:10:29.542
money that built Putin's police state
and his war machine.

00:10:29.584 --> 00:10:31.794
Let us call these things what they are:

00:10:31.794 --> 00:10:34.714
it was appeasement, it was collaboration.

00:10:37.633 --> 00:10:42.180
These days, we prefer to focus
on domestic issues.

00:10:42.597 --> 00:10:43.931
We argue about the past,

00:10:43.973 --> 00:10:45.558
we fantasize about the future

00:10:45.558 --> 00:10:50.521
while ignoring the present.

00:10:51.189 --> 00:10:53.900
Once the move is made

00:10:53.941 --> 00:10:55.610
you cannot change it.

00:10:56.527 --> 00:10:58.821
Acknowledge the wrongdoings of the past,

00:10:58.863 --> 00:11:01.616
but do not pretend it can be fixed.

00:11:02.909 --> 00:11:05.119
It's the present that must be fixed.

00:11:06.871 --> 00:11:09.207
The heroes of the past
were far from perfect.

00:11:09.790 --> 00:11:12.418
But the world we live in
is better because of them.

00:11:12.418 --> 00:11:14.253
We too cannot be perfect.

00:11:14.295 --> 00:11:19.091
But we must always try to be better.

00:11:20.218 --> 00:11:22.678
As a chess player,

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:26.474
I know that strategy is the future
impact of present decisions.

00:11:27.058 --> 00:11:31.938
However grand our plans are
for two, five, even ten moves ahead,

00:11:31.979 --> 00:11:36.609
it's the move that we make now
that determines that future.

00:11:40.238 --> 00:11:44.909
Ukraine is now on the front
line of the war,

00:11:44.951 --> 00:11:49.413
global war of freedom against tyranny.

00:11:51.082 --> 00:11:55.586
The war the free world
didn't want to admit existed.

00:11:56.545 --> 00:11:59.382
It cannot be ignored any longer.

00:12:00.299 --> 00:12:02.551
Brave Ukrainians

00:12:02.593 --> 00:12:05.346
are fighting like hell and dying right now

00:12:05.346 --> 00:12:08.808
to remind us not to take
liberty for granted.

00:12:08.849 --> 00:12:10.434
Putin,

00:12:10.476 --> 00:12:12.603
like every dictator before him,

00:12:12.603 --> 00:12:15.856
underestimated the free will
of free people.

00:12:20.027 --> 00:12:25.783
They deserve every weapon,

00:12:25.825 --> 00:12:28.953
every resource

00:12:28.995 --> 00:12:30.246
to win this war.

00:12:31.122 --> 00:12:32.873
Because they're fighting for us.

00:12:32.915 --> 00:12:36.794
Not only for the whole and free Ukraine.

00:12:38.671 --> 00:12:42.633
Everyone who told me
a decade ago I was wrong,

00:12:42.675 --> 00:12:44.385
now is telling I'm right.

00:12:44.844 --> 00:12:46.053
Unfortunately.

00:12:46.971 --> 00:12:51.892
But we're still
repeating the same mistakes

00:12:51.934 --> 00:12:56.480
of thinking that we can muddle through

00:12:56.522 --> 00:13:00.026
without taking risks,
without taking a stand.

00:13:00.776 --> 00:13:05.656
The price of stopping a dictator
always goes up with every delay,

00:13:05.698 --> 00:13:07.199
every hesitation.

00:13:07.199 --> 00:13:09.410
Meeting evil halfway,

00:13:09.452 --> 00:13:11.454
it's still a victory for evil.

00:13:12.747 --> 00:13:15.666
Evil tempts us with our weakness,

00:13:15.666 --> 00:13:21.756
with our desire for comfort,
being comfortable,

00:13:21.797 --> 00:13:26.802
cautious, rational, civilized.

00:13:28.304 --> 00:13:32.433
What kind of civilization
[are we] fighting for,

00:13:32.475 --> 00:13:36.145
if we allow war crimes and genocide again?

00:13:36.896 --> 00:13:42.026
What kind of world are we leaving
for our children and grandchildren

00:13:42.068 --> 00:13:45.154
if we only talk of the past and the future

00:13:45.196 --> 00:13:50.368
while ignoring murder
and misery in the present?

00:13:53.037 --> 00:13:54.622
This is not chess.

00:13:56.665 --> 00:14:00.669
This is not a battle
between opposite colors,

00:14:00.711 --> 00:14:03.172
but of opposite values.

00:14:03.214 --> 00:14:07.676
Freedom, life and love

00:14:07.718 --> 00:14:10.888
versus tyranny, death and hatred.

00:14:12.598 --> 00:14:15.142
This is not chess.

00:14:15.893 --> 00:14:18.604
But sometimes things are black and white.

00:14:19.188 --> 00:14:22.024
Sometimes you have to fight
for what you believe.

00:14:23.859 --> 00:14:25.194
Or you lose it.

00:14:25.778 --> 00:14:27.238
This is not chess.

00:14:27.988 --> 00:14:33.953
There are no draws, no compromises
in our battle with true evil.

00:14:34.495 --> 00:14:36.122
It's win or lose.

00:14:37.915 --> 00:14:41.252
And so we must fight.

00:14:41.961 --> 00:14:45.339
And so we must win.

00:14:45.673 --> 00:14:47.425
(Ukrainian) Slava Ukraini!

00:14:47.425 --> 00:14:48.801
Glory to Ukraine.

00:14:49.135 --> 00:14:50.469
Glory to freedom.

00:14:50.511 --> 00:14:51.679
Thank you.

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:58.561
(Applause)

